<section class="container py-5" style="max-width: 46rem;">
  <h1 class="h3 mb-3">Terms &amp; Refund Policy</h1>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Registrations</h2>
  <p>Registering for an event reserves your place once payment is confirmed. Your
  place is held against the event's capacity; if an event is sold out you may join
  its waitlist where one is offered.</p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <p>Registrations are <strong>refundable until the event takes place</strong>. You
  can request a refund from your confirmation page or, if you've activated an
  account, from My Registrations. Approved refunds are returned to the original
  payment method by Stripe. If an organiser cancels an event, all confirmed
  registrations are refunded in full automatically.</p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don't use Flyte to commit fraud or to register on someone else's behalf without
  their consent. We may decline or reverse registrations that breach these terms.</p>

  <p class="text-secondary small mt-4">These terms are a plain-language summary for the
  v1 service and may be revised as Flyte grows.</p>
</section>
